-- title:
--   Theorem 4.2, p. 8 — feasible limit points of Algorithm 3.1 satisfying CPLD are KKT points of (2.1); under MFCQ the multiplier estimates are bounded
-- statement:
--   Let $\{x_k\}_{k\in\mathbb N}$ be a sequence generated by the augmented Lagrangian Algorithm 3.1 for problem (2.1),
--   $$\text{minimize } f(x)\quad\text{subject to}\quad h_1(x)=0,\ g_1(x)\le 0,\ h_2(x)=0,\ g_2(x)\le 0,$$
--   with continuously differentiable data. Assume that $x_*\in\Omega_1\cap\Omega_2$ is a limit point of $\{x_k\}$ that satisfies the CPLD constraint qualification with respect to all constraints of (2.1). Then:
--
--   1. $x_*$ is a KKT point of (2.1): there are $\lambda\in\mathbb R^{m_1}$, $\mu\in\mathbb R^{p_1}_+$, $v\in\mathbb R^{m_2}$, $u\in\mathbb R^{p_2}_+$, vanishing on the inequality constraints inactive at $x_*$, with
--   $$\nabla f(x_*)+\sum_{i=1}^{m_1}\lambda_i\nabla[h_1(x_*)]_i+\sum_{i=1}^{p_1}\mu_i\nabla[g_1(x_*)]_i+\sum_{i=1}^{m_2}v_i\nabla[h_2(x_*)]_i+\sum_{j=1}^{p_2}u_j\nabla[g_2(x_*)]_j=0 .$$
--   2. If moreover $x_*$ satisfies MFCQ, then for every subsequence $\{x_k\}_{k\in K}$ converging to $x_*$ the set
--   $$\{\|\lambda_{k+1}\|,\ \|\mu_{k+1}\|,\ \|v_k\|,\ \|u_k\|\}_{k\in K}\tag{4.8}$$
--   is bounded, where $[\lambda_{k+1}]_i=[\bar\lambda_k]_i+\rho_k[h_1(x_k)]_i$ and $[\mu_{k+1}]_i=\max\{0,[\bar\mu_k]_i+\rho_k[g_1(x_k)]_i\}$ are the first-order multiplier estimates of the algorithm and $v_k$, $u_k$ the lower-level multipliers of Step 2.
--
--   The theorem is the main optimality result of the paper: limit points of the method that are feasible are stationary under CPLD, a constraint qualification strictly weaker than MFCQ and LICQ, with no assumption on the penalty parameters.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** "Limit point" is a cluster point of the sequence (`MapClusterPt`); a subsequence $K$ is $x_{\varphi(j)}$ with $\varphi$ strictly increasing, and (4.8) is required for every such subsequence. $\lambda_{k+1}$ and $\mu_{k+1}$ are the unsafeguarded estimates (3.5), (3.7), not the safeguarded $\bar\lambda_{k+1}$, $\bar\mu_{k+1}$, which are bounded by construction. The norms in (4.8) are sup norms (the paper's $\|\cdot\|$ is arbitrary). Both sentences are stated under the theorem's single hypothesis list, as on the page. Problem data, the run, CPLD, MFCQ and KKT are the definitions of `AugLagLLC.KKT.Setting` and `AugLagLLC.KKT.ConstraintQualifications`; the constraints of (2.1) are the families $h_1\oplus h_2$ and $g_1\oplus g_2$.
-- source:
--   Andreani, Birgin, Martínez & Schuverdt, On augmented Lagrangian methods with general lower-level constraints, HAL hal-01295437v1, p. 8, Theorem 4.2 and (4.8)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AugLagLLC_KKT_Setting

namespace AugLagLLC.KKT

open Filter Topology

/-- Theorem 4.2, p. 8: let `{xₖ}` be generated by Algorithm 3.1 and let `xs ∈ Ω₁ ∩ Ω₂` be a limit
point satisfying CPLD with respect to all constraints of (2.1). Then `xs` is a KKT point of (2.1).
Moreover, if `xs` satisfies MFCQ and `x ∘ φ` is any subsequence converging to `xs`, the multiplier
estimates `λₖ₊₁`, `μₖ₊₁`, `vₖ`, `uₖ` (sup norms) are bounded along it ((4.8)). -/
theorem theorem_4_2 {n m1 p1 m2 p2 : ℕ} (P : Problem n m1 p1 m2 p2) (hP : P.IsC1)
    {τ γ ρ1 : ℝ} {lamMin lamMax : Fin m1 → ℝ} {muMax : Fin p1 → ℝ} {ε : ℕ → ℝ}
    (hpar : Problem.IsParams τ γ ρ1 lamMin lamMax muMax ε)
    {x : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)} {ρ : ℕ → ℝ} {lamBar : ℕ → Fin m1 → ℝ}
    {muBar : ℕ → Fin p1 → ℝ} {v : ℕ → Fin m2 → ℝ} {u : ℕ → Fin p2 → ℝ}
    (hrun : P.IsRun τ γ ρ1 lamMin lamMax muMax ε x ρ lamBar muBar v u)
    {xs : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)} (hlim : MapClusterPt xs atTop x)
    (hfeas : xs ∈ P.Omega1 ∩ P.Omega2)
    (hcpld : CPLDAt (Sum.elim P.h1 P.h2) (Sum.elim P.g1 P.g2) xs) :
    IsKKT P.f (Sum.elim P.h1 P.h2) (Sum.elim P.g1 P.g2) xs ∧
      (MFCQAt (Sum.elim P.h1 P.h2) (Sum.elim P.g1 P.g2) xs →
        ∀ φ : ℕ → ℕ, StrictMono φ → Tendsto (x ∘ φ) atTop (𝓝 xs) →
          ∃ C : ℝ, ∀ j, ‖P.lamNext x ρ lamBar (φ j)‖ ≤ C ∧ ‖P.muNext x ρ muBar (φ j)‖ ≤ C ∧
            ‖v (φ j)‖ ≤ C ∧ ‖u (φ j)‖ ≤ C) := by sorry

end AugLagLLC.KKT
